# Allowlist for scripts/deadcode-check.sh.
#
# Each non-comment line is an ERE pattern matched against a raw
# `go tool deadcode -test ./...` report line, which looks like:
#
#   pkg/chains/evm/converter.go:444:21:\t(\*\?evm\.<T>\)\.<Name>
#
# Match on a distinctive part of the symbol name rather than a line
# number, which moves on every edit. Entries exist only for symbols that
# are alive through indirection the analyzer cannot see (reflection,
# dynamic dispatch it does not model); anything genuinely unreachable is
# deleted, never listed. The guard warns when an entry stops matching —
# remove stale ones on sight.
